From: r8q bring-up <r8q@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] r8q: clk: qcom: dispcc-sm8250: don't park the MDP clock at registration

disp_cc_mdss_mdp_clk_src uses clk_rcg2_shared_ops, whose .init parks the RCG
on XO (19.2 MHz) as soon as dispcc registers. On a phone whose bootloader left
the display running (r8q: Samsung XBL lights the S6E3FC3 panel in command mode
with DSC and autorefresh), that starves the DPU a few seconds into boot: the
DSI link sends garbage, the panel shows a flash of colours and then blanks
itself (its TE output stops) until msm re-initialises everything.

Use clk_rcg2_shared_no_init_park_ops, as dispcc-sc8280xp and dispcc-x1e80100
already do for their MDP clocks, so the boot console keeps scanning out
until msm takes over.

---
--- a/drivers/clk/qcom/dispcc-sm8250.c
+++ b/drivers/clk/qcom/dispcc-sm8250.c
@@ -565,7 +565,7 @@
 		.parent_data = disp_cc_parent_data_5,
 		.num_parents = ARRAY_SIZE(disp_cc_parent_data_5),
 		.flags = CLK_SET_RATE_PARENT,
-		.ops = &clk_rcg2_shared_ops,
+		.ops = &clk_rcg2_shared_no_init_park_ops,
 	},
 };
 
